WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:15.471
Maggie Henry and came running over.

2
00:00:15.491 --> 00:00:17.032
"I knew it!"

3
00:00:17.293 --> 00:00:17.773
she cried.

4
00:00:17.793 --> 00:00:19.795
"It was Rebecca, wasn't it?"

5
00:00:19.815 --> 00:00:22.217
"Hold on," Henry said.

6
00:00:22.237 --> 00:00:25.480
"I need to find one last bit of evidence."

7
00:00:29.152 --> 00:00:33.454
Henry ducked into Big Spot's stall and felt around in the bedding until he found something.

8
00:00:35.755 --> 00:00:38.976
Then he hurried out of the stall and down the aisle—right past Rebecca.

9
00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:41.337
Maggie and Cole rushed after him.

10
00:00:41.357 --> 00:00:43.178
"What's going on?"

11
00:00:43.438 --> 00:00:44.198
Maggie demanded.

12
00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:49.261
Henry stopped and quickly told her about how Cole had put the lollipop in Daisy's shirt.

13
00:00:50.381 --> 00:00:51.542
Maggie looked confused.

14
00:00:51.562 --> 00:00:54.063
"So Cole is the shirt thief?"

15
00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:56.844
"Not exactly," Henry said.

16
00:00:57.496 --> 00:01:00.438
"But he's the one who caused the shirt to get stolen."

17
00:01:01.439 --> 00:01:01.920
"I did?"

18
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.041
Cole sounded just as confused as Maggie.

19
00:01:04.061 --> 00:01:06.964
"How?" Henry smiled.

20
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:10.927
"By putting that lollipop in the wrong shirt pocket!"

21
00:01:10.947 --> 00:01:13.169
"Huh?" Cole said.

22
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.452
Henry spotted Daisy and Kira near the lemonade stand.

23
00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:19.754
"Where have you guys been?"

24
00:01:20.014 --> 00:01:20.915
Daisy complained.

25
00:01:20.935 --> 00:01:22.917
"We're thirsty.

26
00:01:23.397 --> 00:01:24.618
Plus it's getting late.

27
00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:26.800
Have you solved the case yet?"

28
00:01:27.596 --> 00:01:28.136
"The case?"

29
00:01:28.477 --> 00:01:29.037
Kira said.

30
00:01:29.057 --> 00:01:30.238
"What case?"

31
00:01:31.258 --> 00:01:32.039
Daisy shrugged.

32
00:01:32.059 --> 00:01:35.260
"Haven't you ever heard of The Lemonade Detectives?

33
00:01:36.121 --> 00:01:38.122
I asked them to find my missing shirt."

34
00:01:39.063 --> 00:01:40.323
"You guys are detectives?"

35
00:01:40.663 --> 00:01:41.704
Kira stared at Henry.

36
00:01:41.724 --> 00:01:44.626
"Is that why you were asking me questions earlier?"

37
00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:48.028
"Yes." Henry noticed that Kira looked pale.

38
00:01:48.048 --> 00:01:50.909
"Is there anything you want to tell Daisy?"

39
00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.111
Kira took a deep breath.

40
00:01:53.731 --> 00:01:55.372
"I do have something to say, Daisy.

41
00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.042
It wasn't your shirt that got ruined.

42
00:01:58.662 --> 00:01:59.423
It was mine!"

43
00:01:59.443 --> 00:02:02.405
"What?" Daisy exclaimed.

44
00:02:02.425 --> 00:02:04.807
"What?" Maggie shrieked.

45
00:02:04.827 --> 00:02:07.069
"Huh?" Cole said.

46
00:02:07.089 --> 00:02:10.732
"Just let Kira explain," Henry told them.

47
00:02:10.752 --> 00:02:15.756
"It all started when Cole put a lollipop in the pocket of the wrong shirt."

48
00:02:16.837 --> 00:02:18.158
Daisy shot a look at Cole.

49
00:02:18.178 --> 00:02:22.221
"I was trying to surprise Daisy," Cole mumbled.

50
00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:25.264
"I didn't know you two had matching shirts."

51
00:02:26.284 --> 00:02:27.204
Daisy smiled.

52
00:02:27.224 --> 00:02:29.445
"Aw, that's sweet.

53
00:02:30.026 --> 00:02:32.927
It almost makes me wish I had a little brother like you!"

54
00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:34.788
Cole looked away.

55
00:02:35.468 --> 00:02:38.809
Henry guessed that Cole didn't like having Daisy treat him like a little brother.

56
00:02:38.829 --> 00:02:43.111
"Kira's stall is right next to Big Spot's," Henry said.

57
00:02:43.131 --> 00:02:48.573
"Close enough for Big Spot to grab Kira's shirt when he smelled that candy."

58
00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:50.074
Kira nodded.

59
00:02:50.094 --> 00:02:53.615
"When I came into the barn earlier, Spot was chewing on my shirt."

60
00:02:54.336 --> 00:02:54.916
She looked away.

61
00:02:56.032 --> 00:02:59.155
"My parents are already mad at me for spending so much money on it.

62
00:02:59.955 --> 00:03:02.397
I knew they'd be even angrier if the shirt got ruined.

63
00:03:03.278 --> 00:03:05.860
I rinsed out most of the horse slobber in the water trough.

64
00:03:06.641 --> 00:03:08.182
But I couldn't get the blue stain out."

65
00:03:08.822 --> 00:03:10.404
She ducked her head, looking ashamed.

66
00:03:10.424 --> 00:03:13.746
"I left my shirt in the water trough and ran inside.

67
00:03:14.987 --> 00:03:19.351
Daisy wasn't around, so I grabbed her shirt and put it on so everyone would think it was

68
00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:26.216
mine." "That explains why you've been wearing your show coat all day despite the heat," Henry guessed.

69
00:03:27.317 --> 00:03:28.417
Kira pulled off her coat.

70
00:03:28.437 --> 00:03:32.538
"I didn't want anyone to notice and figure out the truth," she admitted.

71
00:03:32.558 --> 00:03:37.819
"This stick explains how Big Spot got blue slobber on Maggie's shirt."

72
00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.840
Henry held up the empty lollipop stick he'd found in the pony's stall.

73
00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.001
"This was all that was left of that lollipop."

74
00:03:46.022 --> 00:03:48.502
Kira's eyes filled with tears as she turned to Daisy.

75
00:03:48.522 --> 00:03:50.323
"I'm sorry.

76
00:03:50.723 --> 00:03:51.943
Can you ever forgive me?"

77
00:03:53.003 --> 00:03:54.764
Daisy didn't say anything for a second.

78
00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:56.381
Then she sighed.

79
00:03:56.401 --> 00:04:00.203
"I guess it's partly my fault too," she said.

80
00:04:00.223 --> 00:04:04.246
"I practically forced you to buy that expensive shirt.

81
00:04:05.027 --> 00:04:05.887
I'm sorry.

82
00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.929
Friends?" "Friends."

83
00:04:09.309 --> 00:04:10.530
Kira smiled with relief.

84
00:04:12.231 --> 00:04:13.192
She and Daisy hugged.

85
00:04:13.833 --> 00:04:15.754
Then they linked arms and started walking away.

86
00:04:17.235 --> 00:04:18.456
Suddenly Daisy turned back.

87
00:04:18.476 --> 00:04:22.358
"I almost forgot," she said, digging into her pocket.

88
00:04:22.378 --> 00:04:24.480
"Here's your detective fee.

89
00:04:25.176 --> 00:04:26.637
Thanks for solving the case."

90
00:04:27.818 --> 00:04:28.558
"You're welcome."

91
00:04:29.279 --> 00:04:31.601
Maggie took the money and put it in the cashbox.

92
00:04:33.882 --> 00:04:36.404
"You don't look very excited, Maggie," said Henry.

93
00:04:36.424 --> 00:04:37.905
"What's wrong?"

94
00:04:37.925 --> 00:04:41.667
"I wanted to enter more classes in the show," Maggie said.

95
00:04:41.687 --> 00:04:44.209
"But I still don't have enough money."

96
00:04:44.609 --> 00:04:45.130
She sighed.

97
00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.652
"That's okay, though.

98
00:04:48.252 --> 00:04:50.353
I'll just keep saving money until the next show."

99
00:04:51.274 --> 00:04:53.716
Henry was surprised that Maggie was acting so mature.

100
00:04:54.656 --> 00:04:55.877
He traded a look with Cole.

101
00:04:56.878 --> 00:04:58.058
Then he grabbed the cashbox.

102
00:04:59.039 --> 00:05:01.200
"Here," he said, handing it to Maggie.

103
00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:04.262
"This should be enough to enter more classes."

104
00:05:05.243 --> 00:05:06.424
"Huh?" Maggie said.

105
00:05:06.444 --> 00:05:08.805
"But only a third of that money is mine."

106
00:05:08.825 --> 00:05:11.427
"Not today," Henry said.

107
00:05:12.348 --> 00:05:12.968
Cole nodded.

108
00:05:12.988 --> 00:05:13.869
"Take it, Maggie."

109
00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:16.310
"Wow, thanks!"

110
00:05:17.191 --> 00:05:19.412
Maggie grabbed the cash and took off toward the barn.

111
00:05:19.432 --> 00:05:23.375
"Just don't get used to it!"

112
00:05:23.515 --> 00:05:24.456
Cole called after her.

113
00:05:25.456 --> 00:05:28.060
"Next time it's back to splitting the cash three ways."

114
00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:31.003
Henry laughed.

115
00:05:31.023 --> 00:05:33.907
"I guess that's another case closed."

116
00:05:34.888 --> 00:05:37.592
He pointed to a bunch of thirsty-looking riders heading their way.

117
00:05:37.612 --> 00:05:40.616
"Time to go back to selling lemonade."
